icant","donor_padj":0.790143,"donor_log2fc":0.120304,"donor_lfcse":0.117813,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00409615,"degas_log2fc":-0.138346,"degas_padj":6.88949e-42},{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_symbol":"EGFR","gene_symbol_current":"EGFR","gene_id":"ENSG00000146648","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.635687,"donor_log2fc":0.341461,"donor_lfcse":0.242614,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.011776,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"EGFR","gene_symbol_current":"EGFR","gene_id":"ENSG00000146648","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":1.3513e-24,"nucleus_log2fc":0.328521,"nucleus_score":10.7053,"pct_ad":0.746347,"pct_control":0.697714,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":0.247477,"donor_lfcse":0.168749,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":9.07172e-06,"degas_log2fc":-0.431791,"degas_padj":1.73179e-43},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"EGFR","gene_symbol_current":"EGFR","gene_id":"ENSG00000146648","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.640084,"donor_log2fc":0.428067,"donor_lfcse":0.230534,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00885309,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000146648","module":"greenyellow","kme":0.391303,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.866421,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000146648","module":"black","kme":0.75695,"hub":true,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.655614,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000146648","module":"yellow","kme":0.32744,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.663532,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000146648","entrez_id":["1956"],"uniprot":["P00533"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is a transmembrane glycoprotein that is a member of the protein kinase superfamily. This protein is a receptor for members of the epidermal growth factor family. EGFR is a cell surface protein that binds to epidermal growth factor, thus inducing receptor dimerization and tyrosine autophosphorylation leading to cell proliferation. Mutations in this gene are associated with lung cancer. EGFR is a component of the cytokine storm which contributes to a severe form of Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) resulting from infection with severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus-2 (SARS-CoV-2). [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2020].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P00533","text":"Receptor tyrosine kinase binding ligands of the EGF family and activating several signaling cascades to convert extracellular cues into appropriate cellular responses (PubMed:10805725, PubMed:12297050, PubMed:12620237, PubMed:12873986, PubMed:15374980, PubMed:15590694, PubMed:17115032, PubMed:19560417, PubMed:21258366, PubMed:27153536, PubMed:2790960, PubMed:35538033, PubMed:9488479). Known ligands include EGF, TGFA/TGF-alpha, AREG, epigen/EPGN, BTC/betacellulin, epiregulin/EREG and HBEGF/heparin-binding EGF (PubMed:12297049, PubMed:15611079, PubMed:17909029, PubMed:20837704, PubMed:27153536, PubMed:2790960, PubMed:7679104, PubMed:8144591, PubMed:9419975). Ligand binding triggers receptor homo- and/or heterodimerization and autophosphorylation on key cytoplasmic residues (PubMed:10026169, PubMed:17349580, PubMed:18046415, PubMed:19560417, PubMed:19836242). The phosphorylated receptor recruits adapter proteins like GRB2 which in turn activates complex downstream signaling cascades (PubMed:10026169, PubMed:17349580, PubMed:18046415, PubMed:19560417, PubMed:19836242). Activates at least 4 major downstream signaling cascades including the RAS-RAF-MEK-ERK, PI3 kinase-AKT, PLCgamma-PKC and STATs modules (PubMed:27153536). May also activate the NF-kappa-B signaling cascade (PubMed:11116146). Also directly phosphorylates other proteins like RGS16, activating its GTPase activity and probably coupling the EGF receptor signaling to the G protein-coupled receptor signaling (PubMed:11602604). Also phosphorylates MUC1 and increases its interaction with SRC and CTNNB1/beta-catenin (PubMed:11483589). Positively regulates cell migration via interaction with CCDC88A/GIV which retains EGFR at the cell membrane following ligand stimulation, promoting EGFR signaling which triggers cell migration (PubMed:20462955). Acts as a positive regulator of cGAS-STING signaling by mediating tyrosine phosphorylation of STING1, promoting production of type I interferon (IFN-alpha and IFN-beta), while inhibiting STING1 ability to regulate autophagy (PubMed:32926474). Plays a role in enhancing learning and memory performance (By similarity). Plays a role in mammalian pain signaling (long-lasting hypersensitivity) (By similarity). [Isoform 2]: May act as an antagonist of EGF action. (Microbial infection) Acts as a receptor for hepatitis C virus (HCV) in hepatocytes and facilitates its cell entry. Mediates HCV entry by promoting the formation of the CD81-CLDN1 receptor complexes that are essential for HCV entry and by enhancing membrane fusion of cells expressing HCV envelope glycoproteins."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}